\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{frap}
\title{Positions, orientations, and global constraints}

\p{A [facet move](frap-000L) transports a piece's incident labels
along with its position. Local frames turn this transport into group
coordinates, as in \citet{Section 3.1}{marchetti2025rubik}. We derive
the composition law, a frame-independent total orientation and the
additional test that makes it a conserved quantity for cube face turns.}

